When the buffer is resized, `js_realloc` may return a new pointer if the memory needs to be moved. The old memory is freed, and `abuf->data` is updated to point to the new location at line 56195. However, any raw pointers that were previously captured (like in `js_atomics_op`) are now stale - they point to freed memory.

